  "notes": "USAGE: {転居|てんきょ} is a formal word used mainly in official documents, government forms, and written communication. In everyday conversation, {引|ひ}っ{越|こ}し or {引|ひ}っ{越|こ}す is more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {転居届|てんきょとどけ}: change-of-address notification\n- {転居先|てんきょさき}: new address (after moving)\n- {転居|てんきょ}する: to move, to relocate\n- {転居|てんきょ}の{挨拶|あいさつ}: moving announcement\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {転居|てんきょ}: formal term for changing residence\n- {引|ひ}っ{越|こ}し: moving (everyday term)\n- {移転|いてん}: relocation (used for both residences and businesses/offices)",
